rig-data/
# Next's build output and the type shim it regenerates on every build
# (#129). `.next/` is also an eslint ignore, because `projectService` treats
# a file no tsconfig describes as a parse error rather than a skip.
.next/
# Agent scratch: ticket bodies and specs pulled down for review, never
# committed.
.scratch/
# The live lanes' turn capture (#148). `DITO_EVAL_CAPTURE=<path>` appends
# one JSON line per model call — the turns verbatim, every tool input, the
# usage. It is EVIDENCE for a measurement, read while the numbers are being
# argued about and then thrown away; the artifact that survives is the
# report in `packages/evals/reports/`. It is ignored rather than committed
# for the same reason `rig-data/` is: a capture from the rig would be a
# rep's real conversations, and the difference between a corpus capture and
# a rig one is a flag on a command line.
capture/
# The owner app's SDK child directory (#328), a sibling of its working
# directory: the CLI's own config and cache, never committed.
apps/owner-web.harness/
